						<p class="has-text-align-none">The company <a href="https://hyte.com/events/computex?utm_campaign=computex2026&amp;utm_source=pr&amp;utm_medium=referral">showed off the Y50 RGB</a> during Computex 2026, which costs just $99.99. It supports an array of motherboard sizes and comes with the same three-piece panoramic glass as the <a href="https://hyte.com/store/y70/cs-hyte-y70-tm">pricier Y70</a>.</p>

<p class="has-text-align-none">Hyte is just <a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/937699/will-there-still-be-a-desktop-pc-industry-at-this-rate">one of the PC component makers</a> grappling with the effects of the RAM crunch, and is likely launching this more affordable case to offset surging prices.</p>

