			<title type="html"><![CDATA[Looking clutch.]]></title>
			<link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/941456/looking-clutch" />
			<id>https://www.theverge.com/?post_type=vm_quickpost&#038;p=941456</id>
			<updated>2026-06-02T08:37:53-04:00</updated>
			<published>2026-06-02T08:31:21-04:00</published>
			<category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Entertainment" /><category scheme="https://www.theverge.com" term="Gaming" />
							<summary type="html"><![CDATA[Maverick Games, a studio made up of former Forza developers (which was previously working with Amazon), just teased its first title, an open-world racer called Clutch. It looks like a mixture of Forza and Need For Speed, and the studio will be showing more off at SGF Live on Friday.]]></summary>
			
							<content type="html">
											<![CDATA[

						<p class="has-text-align-none">Maverick Games, a studio made up of former <em>Forza</em> developers (<a href="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/884280/amazon-publishing-deal-maverick-games-forza-cancel" data-type="link" data-id="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/884280/amazon-publishing-deal-maverick-games-forza-cancel">which was previously working with Amazon</a>), just teased its first title, an open-world racer called <em>Clutch</em>. It looks like a mixture of <em><a href="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/929816/forza-horizon-6-review-xbox-pc" data-type="link" data-id="https://www.theverge.com/entertainment/929816/forza-horizon-6-review-xbox-pc">Forza</a></em> and <em>Need For Speed</em>, and the studio will be showing more off <a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/939238/video-game-gaming-events-summer-game-fest-schedule-2026" data-type="link" data-id="https://www.theverge.com/games/939238/video-game-gaming-events-summer-game-fest-schedule-2026">at SGF Live on Friday</a>.</p>
